
 viewwebfile - Report WEB online file metadata.

 Queries the 'wfile' table in PostgreSQL database 'rdadb' and produces a
 file information view/report grouped and filtered by the options you
 choose.

 USAGE:
   viewwebfile [-C] ColumnNames [-O OrderColumnNames]
               <one or more condition options>
               [output and miscellaneous options]
               [> OutputFile] [| lp -d PrinterName]

 BASIC RULES:

   1. -C ColumnNames is required (see COLUMN OPTIONS below).
      The '-C' flag may be omitted if ColumnNames is the first argument.

   2. At least one condition option must be given:
        -a -d -D -e -f -F -g -G -i -l -m -M -n -o -p -r -s -t -T
        -u -v -W -y -Y -z -Z

   3. Negation: for any condition option except -a, prepend '!' between
      the flag and value to invert the filter, e.g. '-o ! DSS'.

   4. Wildcards: condition options that take strings (-e, -f, -G, -i, -l,
      -o, -t, -u, -v) accept SQL wildcards '%' (any chars) and '_' (one
      char).

   5. By default the output is paginated with a header, footer, and
      column titles. Use -w for plain output (no header/totals).


 COLUMN OPTIONS:

   -C ColumnNames
        A string of one or more column letters listed below. The display
        order of columns matches their order in the string. INDEX should
        always be the first column. At least one group column or summary
        column is required.

   -O OrderColumnNames
        Sort the output. Each letter must also appear in -C.
        UPPERCASE = ascending, lowercase = descending.

   Column letters:

     Group Columns:
       A  - CYEAR       - year the file was created
       D  - DATEWRITE   - date the file was last written
       E  - EMAIL       - email of file-written user
       F  - FILENAME    - WEB data file name
       G  - PRODUCT     - product (top group) information
       H  - CMONTH      - month the file was created
       I  - FIRSTNAME   - first name of file-written user
       K  - TIMEWRITE   - time the file was last written
       L  - LASTNAME    - last name of file-written user
       M  - WMONTH      - month the file was last written
       N  - USERNO      - account number of file-written user
       O  - STAT        - file status: Public or Internal
       P  - TYPE        - file type: Data, Software, etc.
       Q  - TIMECREATE  - time the file was created
       R* - DSTITLE     - dataset title
       S  - FILESIZE    - individual file size (bytes)
       T  - DATASET     - dataset name
       U  - USERNAME    - login name of file-written user
       V  - DIV.        - division of file-written user
       W  - DSTYPE      - dataset type flag: P, H, I, or W
       Y  - WYEAR       - year the file was last written
       Z  - DATECREATE  - date the file was created

       (*) = column may be displayed with zero usages when -z is used.

     Summary Columns:
       B - MBYTESFILES  - data size (MB) by the group
       C - #USER        - number of users in the group
       J - #FILE        - number of files by the group

     Index Column:
       X - INDEX        - 1-based row index (use as the first column)


 CONDITION OPTIONS:

   -a   All WEB file metadata in 'wfile'.
   -A RowLimit                       Limit the number of rows returned.
   -d DateList                       Last written on these dates.
   -D StartDate [EndDate]            Last written between two dates.
   -e EMailList                      Last written by users with these emails.
   -f FileNameList                   These WEB file names.
   -F MinFileName [MaxFileName]      File names in this range.
   -g GroupIndices                   These top group indices.
   -G GroupIDs                       These top group IDs.
   -i FirstNameList                  Users with these first names.
   -j                                Include Group IDs in PRODUCT column.
   -J                                Include Group Titles in PRODUCT column.
   -l LastNameList                   Users with these last names.
   -m MonthList                      Last written in these months (YYYY-MM).
   -M MonthList                      Created in these months (YYYY-MM).
   -n UserNumberList                 These user account numbers.
   -o FileStatus                     File status: P (Public) or I (Internal).
   -p TypeList                       File types: D (Data), I (Internal Data),
                                     O (Document), S (Software).
   -r MinIdx [MaxIdx]                Group indices in this range.
   -s MinSize [MaxSize]              File sizes in MB in this range.
   -t DatasetList                    Files in these datasets.
   -T MinDataset [MaxDataset]        Files in datasets in this ID range,
                                     e.g. '-T d540000 d550009'.
   -u UserNameList                   Last written by users with these
                                     login names.
   -v DivisionList                   Last written by users from these
                                     divisions.
   -W DatasetTypes                   Dataset type flag: P, H, I, or W.
   -y YearList                       Last written in these years (YYYY).
   -Y YearList                       Created in these years (YYYY).
   -z DateList                       Created on these dates.
   -Z StartDate [EndDate]            Created between two dates.


 OUTPUT AND MISCELLANEOUS OPTIONS:

   -H Title           Replace the default report title.
   -L Delimiter       Use Delimiter between columns instead of spaces.
   -U SizeUnit        Show sizes in unit: B, K, M, or G.
   -w                 Simple format: no header, no totals.
   > OutputFile       Redirect output to a file.
   | lp -d Printer    Send output to the named printer (e.g. lj100).


 EXAMPLES:

   View files last written in 2004 with columns INDEX, USERNAME, STAT,
   #FILE, MBYTESFILES; sort by STAT ascending and MBYTESFILES descending:

      viewwebfile XUOJB -y 2004 -O Ob

   Restrict to files matching '/DSS/Y%':

      viewwebfile XUOJB -y 2004 -f /DSS/Y% -O Ob

   Same, excluding DSS users, and save to a file:

      viewwebfile XUOJB -y 2004 -f /DSS/Y% -o ! DSS -O Ob > wfile.out
